A||||7||BroCar 87||DEW WIPES (outside door)||||5||
Z||000000||BroCar 87||10-27-2000||06:24 PM||||Where is the best/cheapest place to get them?? How hard are they to replace? <BR>Thanks in advance! <P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature2.jpg">  <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>   Custom dual side exit exhaust!||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||10-27-2000||07:04 PM||||Try your local GM/pontiac dealer(s).||||reg||1
Z||000002||MrPBody||10-27-2000||08:07 PM||||Ditto Ogre.  As far as I know, Pontiac is the only real source, although other vendors re-sell them.  I bought a pair a few months ago for $30-something each.<P>Buying them is the easy part . . .  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||10-27-2000||10:28 PM||||Fiero Store has them. At least for me it has been one of the harder things to install. I did it without removing any rivet or door glass.||||reg||1
Z||000004||hrocker||10-28-2000||05:51 AM||||I just got a pair from Criswell GM Parts, $54.75 for both delivered.<P>1-888-466-9101||||reg||14
Z||000005||mrfixit58||10-28-2000||09:51 AM||||I got mine from the local GM dealer. around $45. I've try it both ways and I found it was MUCH easier to remove the door panel and unbolt the window guides. This allows the window to be pushed forward and rearward to expose the two center screws. Just use the original bolt locations when re-assembling the guides. Once you have a little confidence, it only takes about 45 minutes per side.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||deceler8||10-28-2000||10:21 AM||||I agree...looks like a daunting task, but once you've removed the door panel and loosened the felt pad guides that hold the glass in place, you've only got two screws to worry about (in the center)...the others come out with a regular screwdriver. The forward end of the dew wipe is held by the bolts that secure the mirror, so you do have to remove the mirror.<P>Rodney's dew wipe tool makes the job of removing the center screws that are behind the glass simple. If you don't have one, E-Mail me and I'll mail you mine (I will want it back, LOL).||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bob Englert||10-30-2000||03:46 PM||||There is a good writeup on Dew wipe replacement on the Michigan Fiero Club website at <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/dewstrip.pdf" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/dewstrip.pdf</A> <P>It is in Adobe Acrobat format but you can also download the reader from the same site.<P>Bob<BR>2-87 GT's<BR>87 Coupe<BR>85 SE (For Sale)<BR>||||reg||1
